<xs:schema xmlns:uci="https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" targetNamespace="https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified" version="006.0.ASK">
	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>DISTRIBUTION STATEMENTS

DISCLAIMER: The discussion of non-federal entities, methods, products, or services does not imply any endorsement by the United States Government, the Department of Defense, or the Department of the Air Force.

Distribution Statement A. Approved for public release: distribution is unlimited.
        </xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>
	<!--== START MESSAGES ==-->
	<xs:element name="FlightActivity" type="uci:FlightActivityMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>A [Capability]Activity message describes what a Capability is actively doing  It is generally a complete, coherent snapshot of all Activities for a Capability category (ESM, EA, etc.). In UCI terminology, an Activity is the dynamic, per-use status of a Capability. An Activity is an abstraction that includes the autonomous (MDF-driven or MissionPlan-driven) activity of a Capability.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="FlightCapabilityStatus" type="uci:FlightCapabilityStatusMT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message reports the current status of the Flight capabilities available to the system. This includes information regarding whether or not each capability is currently available based on hardware status, operational states, etc.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="NavigationReport" type="uci:NavigationReportMT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates the current navigation state of the System.  It is one of the "station-keeping" series of messages reported by most UCI Systems.  The station-keeping series is: PositionReport, SystemStatus, NavigationReport, [Capability]Status and [Capability]Activity.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="PositionReport" type="uci:PositionReportMT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates the location and speed of a System or Resource.  It is analogous to a simplified MIL-STD-6016 PPLI message.  It is one of the "station-keeping" series of messages reported by most UCI Systems.  The station-keeping series includes PositionReport, SystemStatus, NavigationReport, [Capability]Status and [Capability]Activity.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="ServiceStatus" type="uci:ServiceStatusMT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates the current status of a service.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="SubsystemStatus" type="uci:SubsystemStatusMT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates a Subsystem's current operating state.  For configuration data use SubsystemConfiguration message.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<xs:element name="SystemStatus" type="uci:SystemStatusMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates the current, highest level summary status of a System, its identification and an indication of the Services, Subsystems and Capabilities it contains.  A System is anything that can self-report information about itself.</xs:documentation>
			<xs:documentation>UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>
	<!--== SUPPORTING TYPES ==-->
	<xs:complexType name="AIS_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MMSI_Number" type="uci:MMSI_NumberStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Maritime Mobile Service Identity (MMSI) number of the vehicle/vessel.  In AIS, MMSI numbers are part of the unique ID of a track and serve as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS MMSI numbers are directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IMO_Number" type="uci:IMO_NumberType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the International Maritime Organization (IMO) identifier number of the vehicle/vessel.  In AIS, IMO numbers are part of the unique ID of a track and serve as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS IMO numbers are directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VesselName" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString20OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the AIS vessel name.  In AIS, vessel name is part of the unique ID of a track and serves as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS vessel name is directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CallSign" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString20Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the AIS radio call sign.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AboutType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Model" type="uci:VisibleString32Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a widely known and coordinated model name for the associated item, generally established at the time of production.  For example, "AN/APG-79".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SerialNumber" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the serial number or other unique identifier assigned to an instance of the Model, generally established at the time of production.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SoftwareVersion" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the installed software/OFP version, for items whose software can be updated post-production without changing the Model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BootloaderSoftwareVersion" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the installed bootloader version.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HardwareVersion" type="uci:VisibleString32Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the installed hardware version, for items whose hardware can be updated post-production without changing the Model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="Acceleration3D_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Acceleration relative to WGS-84 ellipsoid.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NorthAcceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The acceleration component along the true north direction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EastAcceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The acceleration component along the east direction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DownAcceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The acceleration component along the down direction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the date and time at which the acceleration data was measured, last known to be correct and/or predicted to occur.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AccelerationType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates acceleration in meters per second per second (m/s^2).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:double" />
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActionID_Type" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to Actions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:VersionedID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityBaseType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability which the Activity is an instance of.  Generally an Activity is an instance of a single Capability.  An Activity can be associated with multiple Capabilities when, for example, a Subsystem has distinct Capabilities for automated and manual.  In this case, if a manual command is issued while an automated Activity that achieves the desired result already exists, a single Activity represents both Capabilities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Interactive" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether or not the Activity can be edited/modified via a [Capability]Command...Activity message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityState" type="uci:ActivityStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current state of the Activity its state machine.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Basis" type="uci:ActivityBasisEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the basis of the Activity.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  If omitted, a basis of ACTUAL should be assumed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityRank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the rank of the Activity amongst all other Activities of the Capability and/or Subsystem.  This isn't necessarily the same as the Rank associated with the sibling ActivitySource.  This element is meant to convey the Subsystem determined relative ranking of all Activities of a Capability category (ESM, EA, etc.).  For Subsystems with multiple Capability categories this element is meant to convey relative ranking across all Capability categories.  In addition to the rank of the ActivitySource, an Activity's rank can be influenced by Capability priority (see CapabilitySettings), RF_ControlCommands and other factors that influence the Subsystem's internal scheduling and resource allocation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityReason" type="uci:CannotComplyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details regarding the reason for and/or a contributing factor to the sibling ActivityState element.  This element is only expected when the Activity is in a potentially undesirable state such as constrained, failed or completed with less than optimum results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:ActivitySourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an originating "source" of the Activity; the command or other item which invoked this specific Activity of a Capability.  A single Activity can fully or partially satisfy Activity sources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time when the Activity started or is expected to start.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedCompletionTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time when the Activity will complete.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentComplete" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current estimated percent complete of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ActivityBasisEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the basis of a reported Activity.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTUAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activity is an actual one reported first-person or first-person surrogate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SENSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activity is a sensed, third-person activity reported by the sensor or sensor surrogate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PREDICTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activity is a predicted, third-person activity reported by a prediction algorithm.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activity is a planned activity reported by an algorithm that estimates plan execution progress.  A PLANNED activity can be reported when an ACTUAL activity can't due to comms or other limitations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityByType" uci:version="000.000.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the "activity" of the Entity. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUIs 1798/001, 1798/002, 1798/003, 1798/004 and 1798/005 for additional details. In MIL-STD-6016, activity indexes/values vary by environment and therefore this element is only meaningful when paired with the sibling ActivityCategory element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityAmplification" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates amplifying information for the activity of the Entity. See MIL-STD-6016 DFI 752 DUI 001 for additional details. Each environment has a corresponding set of activity amplifications.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityCategory" type="uci:EnvironmentEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the MIL-STD-6016 list/category of the sibling Activity element. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUI 275/004 for additional details. Each environment has a corresponding set of specific types.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CustomActivity" type="uci:ForeignKeyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a custom activity that is supplemental to the sibling Activity element. This element is expected only if a custom activity, which isn't included or fully described by MIL-STD-6016 can be identified. In that case, the sibling Activity Element indicates "no statement" or the closest match and this element completes the activity characterization.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivitySubCategory" type="uci:ActivitySubCategoryEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of track being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to *Capability Activities.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityPlanID_Type" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type is the standard UCI ID type that corresponds to an ActivityPlan.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:VersionedID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityPlanReferenceType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActivityPlanID" type="uci:ActivityPlansID_ChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *ActivityPlan that is the source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MissionPlanID" type="uci:MissionPlanID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the MissionPlan associated with the sibling *ActivityPlan.  If the referenced *ActivityPlan is part of multiple MissionPlans, this element indicates the specific MissionPlan context desired.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlannedActivityID" type="uci:PlannedActivityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Planned Activity in the sibling *ActivityPlan that is a source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityPlansID_ChoiceType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="RouteActivityPlanID" type="uci:RouteActivityPlanID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the RouteActivityPlan that is the source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitActivityPlanID" type="uci:OrbitActivityPlanID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the OrbitActivityPlan that is the source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityPlanID" type="uci:ActivityPlanID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the ActivityPlan that is the source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivitySourceType" uci:version="001.000.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Requirement" type="uci:RequirementInstanceID_ChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Requirement that is the source or cause of the Activity.  For example, a Task could be the direct source of an Activity when the Subsystem which implements the associated Capability monitors Tasks to determine when to initiate Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MDF" type="uci:MDF_ReferenceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a MDF that is the source or cause of the Activity.  A MDF could be the direct source of an Activity when the Subsystem which implements the associated Capability has MDF configurable/driven automation of its Capabilities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityPlan" type="uci:ActivityPlanReferenceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a *ActivityPlan that is the source or cause of the Activity.  A *ActivityPlan could be the direct source of an Activity when the Subsystem which implements the associated Capability directly follows along with a System *ActivityPlan to determine when to initiate Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedMessage" type="uci:AssociatedMessageSourceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an associated message that is the source or cause of the Activity.  For example, a SettingsCommand could be the direct source of an Activity when the Subsystem utilizes Settings to determine when to initiate Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ActivityStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This enumerated type represents the state machine for an Activity.  Additional details including allowed transitions are given in the accompanying UML model for the Activity state machine.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity is disabled.  This is a default or commanded state.  A DISABLED Activity can't become ACTIVE_* unless it is first ENABLED via the associated [Capability]SettingsCommand.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ENABLED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity is enabled.  This is a default or commanded state.  An ENABLED Activity is free to transition to ACTIVE_* and other states at the discretion of the host Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVE_UNCONSTRAINED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity is currently being performed and isn't performance limited by resource limitations or other constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVE_PARTIALLY_CONSTRAINED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity is currently being performed but performance is being limited by resource limitations or other constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVE_FULLY_CONSTRAINED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates triggering conditions for the Activity currently exist but the Activity isn't being performed due to resource limitations or other constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity was ACTIVE_* and finished.  This is a termination state for the Activity state machine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity was ENABLED and was possibly ACTIVE_* but failed prior to being COMPLETED.  This is a termination state for the Activity state machine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DELETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Activity was deleted.  This is a termination state for the Activity state machine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ActivitySubCategoryEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Expresses the type of track being reported.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="SUBSURFACE_TRACK">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A Subsurface Track is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SURFACED_SUBMARINE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A Surfaced Submarine Track is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SNORKELING_SUBMARINE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A Snorkeling Submarine Track is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DATUM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A DATUM is being reported.</xs:documentation>
