	<xs:complexType name="PolygonType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies a polygon.  The vertices of the polygon can be specified by geospatial locations or as locations relative to a separately defined reference frame.
Simple polygons (including those in which interior polygons are defined within a bounding polygon) are supported.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="LineProjection" type="uci:LineProjectionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of lines that form the BoundingPolygon and any InteriorPolygon definitions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BoundingPolygon" type="uci:PolygonPointChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Geospatial points defining the vertices of a simple polygon (i.e closed and non-intersecting).  These points are ordered and assumed to be unique.  Closure is assumed between the final point and the first point. Smaller polygon areas within the BoundingPolygon can be excluded from its functional/operational purpose using the sibling InteriorPolygon element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InteriorPolygon" type="uci:PolygonPointChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Geospatial points defining the vertices of a simple polygon (i.e closed and non-intersecting) whose vertices lie wholly inside the BoundingPolygon and whose edges do not intersect with other InteriorPolygon definitions.  These points are ordered and assumed to be unique.  Closure is assumed between the final point and the first point.  The area within an InteriorPolygon is functionally/operationally equivalent to the area outside the sibling Bounding Polygon.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
